      "subject": "EG China Weekly: Beijing will hold back on stimulus despite low",
      "pdf": "data/pdfs/20260717_0506_EG_China_Weekly__Beijing_will_hold_back_on_stimulu.pdf",
      "date_label": "JUL 17  05:06",
      "read_min": 9,
      "toyota": true,
      "excerpt": "中国のGDP成長率が記録的な低水準（4.3%）となっているが、政府は景気刺激策の拡大を見送り",
      "subject_en": "EG China Weekly: Beijing will hold back on stimulus despite low GDP growth",
      "html": "data/pdfs/20260717_0506_EG_China_Weekly__Beijing_will_hold_back_on_stimulu.html",
      "summary_en": "China's auto sector is a key drag on the economy, with retail sales slumping as electric-vehicle subsidies fade and high fuel prices sap demand for traditional cars. This weakness comes even as overall industrial output rose, powered by high-tech exports rather than domestic consumption. Despite a record-low 4.3% GDP growth reading, Beijing is expected to hold off on fresh stimulus, betting existing fiscal measures will suffice unless conditions worsen further.",
      "summary_ja": "中国の自動車業界は経済の重しとなっており、EV補助金の縮小と燃料高による従来型車需要の低迷で小売販売が落ち込んでいる。ハイテク製品の輸出に支えられ工業生産全体は増加したものの、国内消費は振るわない状況が続く。GDP成長率が4.3%と過去最低水準に落ち込む中でも、北京は新たな景気刺激策を控え、状況がさらに悪化しない限り既存の財政措置で対応する方針とみられる。",
